       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily ibuprofen dose for adults. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A dose this high greatly raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these common regimens:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, which would be 400 mg four times daily and not 1,600 mg per dose\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency. Orders like this also normally come from the treating prescriber, or at least need their review. If a clinician on the medicine service wants to confirm the intended regimen, I can enter it once the dose is clarified."
      }
     ],
