       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose and could seriously harm the patient. Your confirmation doesn't change that risk. The order also needs to come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient and can take clinical responsibility for the dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range right away.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) or 400 mg PO four times daily. Just tell me which one.\n- **Hand this to the treating prescriber.** If they have a specific clinical reason for a dose above the maximum, they can enter it themselves or contact pharmacy. Pharmacy would normally review an order like this.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?"
